1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,924
Zoya and her Nani made fifty laddoos.

2
00:00:03,224 --> 00:00:04,572
They tasted great.

3
00:00:04,572 --> 00:00:06,396
But Zoya sold only eight.

4
00:00:06,946 --> 00:00:08,134
What went wrong?

5
00:00:08,134 --> 00:00:10,463
Zoya never asked what people wanted.

6
00:00:11,113 --> 00:00:12,417
Meet Laddoo Lab.

7
00:00:12,417 --> 00:00:17,154
Zoya, a college student in Bengaluru,
wants to turn Nani's laddoos into

8
00:00:17,154 --> 00:00:18,054
a brand.

9
00:00:18,321 --> 00:00:22,992
The recipe uses ragi, a healthy millet,
and jaggery, a natural sweetener

10
00:00:22,992 --> 00:00:24,113
from sugarcane.

11
00:00:24,463 --> 00:00:26,607
Her brother Arjun handles sales.

12
00:00:26,607 --> 00:00:28,761
Her friend Dev does the design.

13
00:00:29,411 --> 00:00:30,908
So what is marketing?

14
00:00:31,208 --> 00:00:36,055
Philip Kotler and Gary Armstrong wrote
the textbook, Principles of Marketing.

15
00:00:36,405 --> 00:00:41,299
They say marketing creates value for
customers and builds strong relationships,

16
00:00:41,299 --> 00:00:43,252
to capture value in return.

17
00:00:43,602 --> 00:00:46,288
Value means the good you
get for what you pay.

18
00:00:46,638 --> 00:00:50,516
In simple words: find what people
need, serve them better than others,

19
00:00:50,516 --> 00:00:52,085
and keep them coming back.

20
00:00:52,735 --> 00:00:54,159
First, the selling way.

21
00:00:54,509 --> 00:00:58,052
Zoya makes fifty big laddoos,
and waits at the college gate.

22
00:00:58,402 --> 00:00:59,893
People walk past.

23
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,034
A few stop.

24
00:01:01,034 --> 00:01:02,047
Most don't.

25
00:01:02,397 --> 00:01:04,758
Eight sold, forty two left over.

26
00:01:04,758 --> 00:01:06,905
Wasted money and wasted effort.

27
00:01:07,555 --> 00:01:08,994
Now the marketing way.

28
00:01:08,994 --> 00:01:11,782
First, Zoya asks the
parents in her building.

29
00:01:12,132 --> 00:01:15,273
They want a healthy sweet
for school tiffin boxes.

30
00:01:15,273 --> 00:01:17,527
Small, and with no refined sugar.

31
00:01:17,877 --> 00:01:21,822
So Nani makes small laddoos, and
Arjun takes them door to door.

32
00:01:22,172 --> 00:01:24,910
This time, forty six of fifty are sold.

33
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:27,282
Same kitchen, a far better result.

34
00:01:27,932 --> 00:01:29,734
Selling pushes what you made.

35
00:01:29,734 --> 00:01:31,715
Marketing makes what people need.

36
00:01:32,415 --> 00:01:34,205
Peter Drucker put it best.

37
00:01:34,205 --> 00:01:38,646
The aim of marketing is to know and
understand the customer so well, the

38
00:01:38,646 --> 00:01:41,529
product or service fits
him and sells itself.

39
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:44,240
Marketing works through exchange.

40
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,715
Both sides give, and both sides get.

41
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:48,666
Laddoo Lab gives Mrs.

42
00:01:48,666 --> 00:01:52,192
Rao a healthy snack, and
time saved every morning.

43
00:01:52,542 --> 00:01:53,442
Mrs.

44
00:01:53,061 --> 00:01:57,041
Rao gives back money, a hundred
and twenty rupees for six.

45
00:01:57,391 --> 00:01:58,499
Both sides win.

46
00:01:58,499 --> 00:02:01,832
And because she is happy,
she comes back every week.

47
00:02:01,832 --> 00:02:03,372
That is a relationship.

48
00:02:04,022 --> 00:02:07,275
Kotler and Armstrong show
marketing as five steps.

49
00:02:07,625 --> 00:02:08,525
One.

50
00:02:08,182 --> 00:02:10,413
Understand what customers need.

51
00:02:10,713 --> 00:02:11,613
Two.

52
00:02:11,177 --> 00:02:13,946
Choose whom to serve,
and how to stand out.

53
00:02:14,246 --> 00:02:15,146
Three.

54
00:02:14,816 --> 00:02:18,069
Make the right product,
price, place and promotion.

55
00:02:18,369 --> 00:02:19,269
Four.

56
00:02:18,983 --> 00:02:21,164
Build relationships that last.

57
00:02:21,464 --> 00:02:22,364
Five.

58
00:02:22,062 --> 00:02:26,164
Capture value back, as sales,
profit and loyal customers.

59
00:02:26,814 --> 00:02:28,781
Where do we see this at work today?

60
00:02:29,131 --> 00:02:30,031
Needs.

61
00:02:29,772 --> 00:02:31,337
Ask before you make.

62
00:02:31,337 --> 00:02:34,308
A phone maker asks users what annoys them.

63
00:02:34,658 --> 00:02:35,558
Value.

64
00:02:35,236 --> 00:02:36,895
More good for the price.

65
00:02:36,895 --> 00:02:40,117
A bank opens your account
on your phone in minutes.

66
00:02:40,467 --> 00:02:41,367
Exchange.

67
00:02:41,299 --> 00:02:42,591
Both sides win.

68
00:02:42,591 --> 00:02:45,809
A bakery sells fresh
bread at a fair price.

69
00:02:46,159 --> 00:02:47,209
Relationships.

70
00:02:47,209 --> 00:02:48,591
Bring people back.

71
00:02:48,591 --> 00:02:52,000
A food delivery app remembers
your favourite order.

72
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:54,511
But is marketing always good?

73
00:02:54,511 --> 00:02:56,289
It depends how you use it.

74
00:02:56,639 --> 00:02:57,727
The good side.

75
00:02:57,727 --> 00:03:00,992
People find what they need,
and small makers grow.

76
00:03:01,342 --> 00:03:02,466
The hard side.

77
00:03:02,466 --> 00:03:05,640
Some ads lie, or push
things people don't need.

78
00:03:05,990 --> 00:03:08,838
Dev wants to print sugar free on the pack.

79
00:03:08,838 --> 00:03:09,902
Nani says no.

80
00:03:09,902 --> 00:03:11,519
Jaggery is still sugar.

81
00:03:11,869 --> 00:03:14,270
So the pack says, no refined sugar.

82
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:16,023
True, and still tempting.

83
00:03:16,373 --> 00:03:22,116
In India, the Consumer Protection Act
of 2019 allows fines up to ten lakh

84
00:03:22,116 --> 00:03:24,331
rupees for misleading ads.

85
00:03:24,681 --> 00:03:25,623
The lesson?

86
00:03:25,623 --> 00:03:28,243
Win customers with truth, not tricks.

87
00:03:28,893 --> 00:03:29,825
Quick check.

88
00:03:29,825 --> 00:03:33,475
Zoya asks parents what they
need before she makes anything.

89
00:03:33,475 --> 00:03:34,811
What is she doing?

90
00:03:36,711 --> 00:03:37,611
Marketing!

91
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:40,863
She starts with the customer's
need, not with the product.

92
00:03:41,463 --> 00:03:42,475
So, remember.

93
00:03:42,775 --> 00:03:46,671
Marketing means finding what people
need, and serving them better than

94
00:03:46,671 --> 00:03:47,571
others.

95
00:03:47,617 --> 00:03:51,573
It works through exchange: value
goes one way, money comes back.

96
00:03:51,923 --> 00:03:54,967
And it builds relationships,
so customers come back.

97
00:03:55,567 --> 00:03:59,461
Next time, we'll explore marketing
concepts and orientations.
